+   Fix, in both places: keep each pushed chunk as its own std::string in a
+   std::deque (a deque never relocates existing elements when you push/pop
+   at an end, so appending never copies or grows a prior allocation) and
+   walk the chunk list with this one `ChunkSource` to serve `Source::read`
+   calls — same bytes, same order, same EOF semantics as a `StringSource`
+   over the concatenation would give, but the largest single allocation is
